[VERDICT — the pin's decision rule (§2), applied]
  T1  [FALSIFIED]  — as PRE-REGISTERED.  The full event poset is not a rooted forest: 23016 register-word classes carry an element whose principal down-set is not a chain (an arb consumes a component of mutually conflicting proposals).
  T2  [THEOREM]  — hypothesis GATED (zero violations, 23226 incomparable arb pairs live) and implication MACHINE-VERIFIED grammar-independently over 46233 rooted forests.  The arb-induced subposet is a rooted forest, hence has order dimension <= 2 and contains no crown, at EVERY width and depth.
  T3  [OPEN — ROUTE FALSIFIED]  — the pin's route to full-poset S3-impossibility is DEAD.  L3 fails (23844 counterexamples): a causal link can be carried entirely by a minted vname register, so x < y does NOT force the actor-register sets to intersect.  L1 fails (16842 of 42144): domination is TRANSITIVE, so a proposal reading a minted vname inherits the arb's whole down-set and a NON-ARB can dominate two incomparable elements.  The FULL-POSET crown claim therefore stands exactly where D44c left it — EVIDENCE AT TESTED SCALE (zero crowns over the three exhaustive families), not a scale-free no-go.
  WHAT IS AND IS NOT FALSIFIED: this receipt falsified ITS OWN reconstruction of the round's argument.  The round's stated route goes through POOL LAMINARITY, was never written in gateable form, and is NOT tested here.  Nothing above impugns the referee's claim; it establishes only that the obvious register-theoretic route to it does not exist.
  SCOPE, per pin §3: clauses (i)-(v) are ALL-SCALE per LOG #354; T2's hypothesis is gated over the three committed families and its implication is machine-verified grammar-independently, so T2 is scale-free in the implication and family-gated in the hypothesis — stated that way, without rounding up.
  PAPER 32 §6 item 7: AMEND TO PARTIAL — the two halves of #355's entry condition (the sixth clause, up-cone confinement) ARE now receipt-gated, and the arb-scoped crown no-go IS now a theorem with a constructive certificate; but §3.1's FULL-POSET claim is NOT discharged and its referee-carried status must be RETAINED, with the note's dead route recorded so no one walks it again.

